declares `license = "MIT OR Apache-2.0"` and `authors = ["Guoqing Bao"]` in `Cargo.toml` and ships **no
LICENSE file and no copyright year** at that commit, so no upstream licence text can be reproduced;
this directory's `LICENSE-MIT` / `LICENSE-APACHE` are baracuda's own.

Per-file status against that commit (measured 2026-10-14 by comparing after stripping comments and
whitespace; earlier text of this NOTICE called four of these "verbatim", which did not hold):

    src/source.rs        — code-identical
    src/compute_cap.rs   — modified (33 lines differ)
    src/parallel.rs      — modified (43 lines differ)
    src/hash.rs          — modified (41 lines differ; cache filename rebranded)
    src/dependency.rs    — modified (104 lines differ; cache directory env var rebranded)
    src/builder.rs       — modified (378 lines differ; cpp_std() added, toolkit detection routed
                           through baracuda-build)
    src/error.rs, src/toolkit.rs, src/lib.rs — exist upstream, modified

Each module carries an `// Origin:` line to the same effect.

We're grateful to Guoqing Bao for releasing cudaforge under permissive terms
and making the work available to the Rust GPU community.
